<title>CHINA: Taiwan-invested shopping centre opens in Shanghai.</title>
<headline>Taiwan-invested shopping centre opens in Shanghai.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>A shopping centre with investment of $29 million by 12 Taiwan chain stores opened for business in Shanghai, the Xinhua news agency said on Monday.</p>
<p>Yaxin Life Plaza is a joint venture between the Taiwan Chain Store Association and the Kunlun Plaza of Shanghai, Xinhua said.</p>
<p>More than 200 firms and retailers from overseas have leased space in the 45,000-square-metre plaza, it said.</p>
</text>
